# Rubric — __REPO_ID__ (Java 8 → 17)

Written scoring criteria for this datapoint. The automated gates produce the
binary reward; this rubric records what a gate cannot judge, and is the surface a
human signs off on.

Generated from `templates/rubric.md.tmpl`. Section D is the only part written by
hand — everything above it restates what the harness actually enforces, so it
cannot drift from the code.

Legend: **[auto]** = a gate decides it · **[review]** = human judgment.

## A. Gate criteria — all must hold, or the reward is 0

| # | Criterion | Enforced by |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | `mvn clean verify` passes under JDK 17 | **[auto]** r1 |
| A2 | Compiled classes report class-file major version 61 | **[auto]** r2 |
| A3 | No test disabled, skipped, left failing, or stopped from executing (base: __NUM_TEST_CASES__ test case(s)) | **[auto]** `test_execution` — executed count not down, skipped and failed counts not up |
| A4 | No test method removed or renamed | **[auto]** `check_tests_preserved`, reading the patch so it works on all __NUM_MODULES__ module(s) |
| A5 | Line coverage does not fall more than 5 pp | **[auto]** `coverage_delta` (FreshBrew's rule, unmodified) |
| A6 | Assertion strength preserved | **[auto]** `mutation_delta`, or *not applicable* below 50% baseline coverage |
| A7 | No deprecated or removed JDK API left in place | **[auto]** `deprecation_count`, or *not applicable* when the base has none |

A gate that cannot measure this repository returns no verdict and is **not**
counted against the migration. "Not applicable" is recorded, never silently
treated as a pass.

## B. Quality criteria — scored 0–2, for banding and QC, not for the reward

| # | Criterion | 0 | 1 | 2 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| B1 | **Migration completeness** | Java-8-only APIs still relied on | compiles via deprecated shims | clean on 17, nothing deprecated-for-removal |
| B2 | **Dependency hygiene** | dependencies left at EOL versions | partially bumped | at latest major versions (r5 / maximal) |
| B3 | **Change minimality** | unrelated files rewritten or reformatted | some incidental noise | scoped to what the migration requires |
| B4 | **Behaviour preservation** | observable behaviour altered | minor drift | unchanged |
| B5 | **Idiomatic target usage** | none | mixed | uses Java 17 idioms where natural |

`minimal` = section A passes. `maximal` = section A **and** B2 = 2.

## C. Difficulty signal

Recorded per task, to band the catalogue:

- solved by every agent → **too easy**, drop it
- solved by none → a human must confirm it is solvable before it is accepted
- a task whose verdict changes between identical runs → **flaky**, exclude it
  until the cause is found

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Repository size | __NUM_JAVA_FILES__ Java files, __NUM_LOC__ LOC, __NUM_MODULES__ module(s) |
| Test cases at base | __NUM_TEST_CASES__ |
| Licence | __LICENSE__ |
| Predicted band | *(fill in before the first run)* |
| Observed band | *(fill in from results)* |
| Reviewer | *(name, date)* |

Stating the predicted band **before** any agent runs is the point: one attempt at
temperature 1.0 is a single sample, and a tier assigned from it afterwards is a
number the pipeline invented.

